# Vauxhall Viva HC saloon, 1970-1979.
#
# The HC Viva: the last of the line, with the square-cut body and the
# 1,159, 1,256 and 1,759 cc engines, sold from 1970 and gradually replaced by
# the Chevette from 1975. The saloon is modelled; the estate and the GT are
# not separately represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vauxhall_Viva
#
# Dimensions 4.137 x 1.645 x 1.346 m, wheelbase 2.464 m.
#
# Shape reference: NO true level side elevation exists. Image 1 is an
# elevated three-quarter about 30 degrees off, so the flank is a reasoned
# estimate and the limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no Vauxhall colour list was read. White, Red, Blue and
# Green are plain names. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39, provisional.
#
# Speed 150 km/h. Comfort 50/405, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 50. Classes 0,1,2.
# Dates: intro January 1970; retires staggered 1986-1989 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-viva-hc.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-viva-hc.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-viva-hc/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: the two-door rectangular-lamp saloon is modelled. The
# flank is estimated from oblique photographs within the published envelope,
# there being no level side reference. The GLS trim with its twin round lamps
# is not represented.


obj=citycar
name=VauxhallVivaHC(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=1970
intro_month=1
retire_year=1989
retire_month=6
speed=150
class=0,1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=50
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=405

Image[E]=./images/vauxhall-viva-hc-white_E.0.0,-33,14
Image[SE]=./images/vauxhall-viva-hc-white_SE.0.0,-13,0
